{
  "version": 2,
  "$comment": "Where the HUD elements sit in each scene. Every element is anchored to an edge pair anchor = '<h>-<v>', h = left|right|center|stretch, v = top|bottom|center|stretch; the offsets are dp from the SAFE AREA (the system bars; the display cutout is ignored, elements may lie under it): `left`/`right` for h = left/right and `top`/`bottom` for v = top/bottom, `x`/`y` = shift from the centre line for center; stretch = both edges given, the box grows and shrinks with the screen (fleet and officer columns wrap into more columns on short screens, the sail lever shrinks to fit under the minimap / compass). width/height only where the element has a fixed box (otherwise the component sizes itself): dp, or a string '<n>%' of the safe area; maxWidth/maxHeight bound it the same way. The land `move` element and the sea `walk` element are ZONES of floating move sticks, drawn under every other element (first in the list; the overlap check lets them lie under the others, the stick at rest must be clear of them): the stick rests at restLeft/restBottom inside it and appears under the thumb that lands anywhere in the zone where no other control is (the deck walk zone: the whole left part, above and beside the helm, which keeps its own touches). props = static props; sample = example live values (bars, counts, fills, lists) for the gallery, the game supplies the real ones. children = components inside the element. behavior = one more touch behaviour of that element (hold: reports down / up; swipe: a drag picks a move, configured by `data`, which becomes data-* attributes). the spyglass (a toggle: one tap raises it, the next lowers it; meanwhile a drag anywhere looks around) sits on the left at sea, below the fleet column and above the helm, in the column where the land fight has its block (the fleet column ends above it); the abilities button sits in the bottom row at sea and, on land, in the potion's place of the action cluster: a tap lays its entries out as HUD buttons in a row left of it (the ship abilities abilities-1…4 at sea; the potion, then Rush in a fight, abilities-1…2 on land), which take the place of the buttons under them (camera and time at sea, travel and the hint on land) until the row folds; the time button (the game's time acceleration in four steps) sits at the bottom, left of the control cluster, at sea and on the world map; walk = the move stick above the helm while the camera is on deck (first person). The sea and world-map helm floats too, up and down only (floatAxis y): its element is a zone as tall as the land move zone and a thumb anywhere in it takes the helm at the thumb's height (never below its rest), the helm keeping its rest left; across it steers by where the thumb is from the helm's middle from the first contact on (the middle straight ahead, either end and beyond full rudder); the zone is `clear` (the overlap check takes the whole box) but for the elements named in `under`, listed after it and drawn over it, which keep their own touches (the fleet, the spyglass, the event lines, the world map's details plate): the resting helm must be clear of them. First person on deck it stays where it rests (the engine sets `fixed`) and only the walk stick floats: `offWith` names the walk, so the walk stick at rest is checked against the resting helm, not its zone. The sail lever stays where it is drawn: a finger takes the position it lands on (at sea), or holds SailUp / SailDown while pushed up or down (the world map). gallery: false = shown only while the game asks for it (the sword-move wheel, the ammunition fan ammo-1…3, which takes the place of the context, camera and abilities buttons, the abilities row abilities-1…4), not on the generated gallery page. c-notice place=hud positions itself in the top-centre band (every toast and game message is at the top); `hint` (c-notice variant hint) is the steady contextual line at the bottom, from the move stick at rest to the action buttons (it only shows, so it may lie over the move zone): where the door ahead leads, whom the talk button talks to — shown exactly while it applies. The pack copy adds `rcss` to every element: the ready position style for an element placed inside c-scene, whose HUD layer is the safe area.",
  "reference": {"width": 915, "height": 412},
